From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0354-lichii-gpu-0216-list-fast.patch

Source: 0354-lichii-gpu-0216-list-fast.patch
dma_pusher: skip the writer wait once written pages settle (EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST, off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Needs 0211 before it.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 179 (tibzejoker), head 3ce0ab7106, GPL-3.0-or-later.

Before each GP entry the front waits for queued compute and copies, because they may write the list
for the first time. =1 skips that once no page was newly marked for 2 s. =2 still waits and logs
each entry the skip would have read too early. The PR's =2 skips as well; ours does not.
Stricter than the PR: nothing counts as settled before the first written page, also in a new session.

Lichii logged 0 misses in 590,000 entries, in one scene. That says little about other scenes.

Runs on the PS5: yes.
Hang: =2 cannot add one. =1 can: a miss is a stale command list. Stale draw arguments lost the device
in Fast Fusion, and a narrower list wait crashed Mario Kart on this console. Use =1 only after whole
sessions of =2 with no miss, and never on Mario Kart. Pool memory: none.
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile before the review changes, Mac-target after them. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
index 9561d522d4..dc410984be 100644
--- a/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/dma_pusher.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,46 @@ static bool ListDrainFull() {
     return full;
 }
 
+// EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST, from Lichii PR 179 (zortos293/Lichii, head 3ce0ab7106). The wait for queued
+// compute and copies before each entry only finds a list page that work writes for the first time:
+// once no page was newly written for 2 s, =1 takes the set of written pages as settled and skips
+// it. =2 still waits and logs each entry the skip would have read too early (the PR's =2 skips
+// too). A miss is a stale command list: Fast Fusion's stale draw arguments lost the device, and a
+// narrower wait crashed Mario Kart World on the console (docs/MKW-TITLE-FPS.md). Keep to =2 until
+// a whole session logs no miss.
+static int ListFastMode() {
+    static const int mode = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST");
+        return value == nullptr ? 0 : value[0] - '0';
+    }();
+    return mode;
+}
+
+bool DmaPusher::WrittenPagesSettled() {
+    const u64 marks = Tegra::g_nx2_new_written_pages.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    const u64 now = static_cast<u64>(Common::g_wall_clock.GetTimeNS().count());
+    if (marks != list_fast_marks) {
+        list_fast_marks = marks;
+        list_fast_since = now;
+        return false;
+    }
+    // No page written yet is not settled: the first dispatch's list would be read too early.
+    return marks != 0 && now - list_fast_since >= 2'000'000'000ULL;
+}
+
+void DmaPusher::NoteListFastCheck(GPUVAddr address, bool written) {
+    static std::atomic<u64> checks{};
+    static std::atomic<u64> misses{};
+    const u64 count = checks.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+    if (written && misses.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) < 16) {
+        LOG_WARNING(HW_GPU, "List fast check: entry at {:#x} became GPU-written", address);
+    }
+    if ((count & 0xffff) == 0) {
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "List fast check: {} waits, {} misses", count,
+                 misses.load(std::memory_order_relaxed));
+    }
+}
+
 bool DmaPusher::Step() {
     if (!ib_enable || dma_pushbuffer.empty()) {
         return false;
@@ -221,10 +261,16 @@ bool DmaPusher::Step() {
         // billions of instances and lost the device loading a race).
